  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "My, your, his/her",
     "texto": [
      "French possessives change depending on whether the thing owned is masculine, feminine or plural.",
      "**mon père** (my father), **ma mère** (my mother), **mes parents** (my parents).",
      "The same with «your»: **ton, ta, tes**. And with «his or her»: **son, sa, ses**.",
      "Watch out: **son frère** can mean «his brother» or «her brother». What matters is the gender of the thing owned, not of the owner.",
      "Before a feminine singular noun that starts with a vowel or a silent **h**, you use **mon, ton, son**: **mon amie** (my female friend)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Possessives",
     "columnas": [
